% Generate `desktop/preload.js`: the locked-down Electron context-bridge preload
% for the OpenNolan window.
%
% The UI reaches the backend over HTTP on the same origin (see `main.js`), so the
% renderer needs nothing from Node — expose ONLY diagnostics + the auto-update
% channel. Keep it minimal: anything added here widens the renderer's privileges.
%
% `'use strict'`, CommonJS `require('electron')` for `contextBridge`, `ipcRenderer`.
% `contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld('openNolan', { ... })` with:

- `desktop: true` — lets the renderer detect it's running in the app.
- `versions: { electron, chrome, node }` from `process.versions`.
- `update` — the auto-update bridge the in-app "update ready" banner consumes
  (`web/src/UpdateBanner.jsx`). Channels must match `main.js`'s IPC handlers, which
  only exist in a packaged build; in dev/browser `getState()` rejects harmlessly and
  the banner stays hidden.
  - `getState()` — `ipcRenderer.invoke('update:get-state')`; resolves `{version}` or null.
  - `install()` — `ipcRenderer.invoke('update:install')`; restart + install the staged build.
  - `onDownloaded(cb)` — subscribe to `'update:downloaded'` via an `(_e, info) => cb(info)`
    listener; RETURN an unsubscribe fn that `removeListener`s it.
